    {
      "id": "library/10665-342236/blocks/prose-sec-007",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Replenishing the CFE",
      "pageStart": 11,
      "pageEnd": 13,
      "target": "../sections/sec-007-replenishing-the-cfe.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The CFE was conceived by Member States and launched \nin 2015 as a revolving fund. Costs initially incurred against \nCFE allocations would be reimbursed by donor funding to \nthe WHO emergency response at country level and unspent \nfunds would be returned. In practice, it has proven difficult \nto raise the level of resources required at country level \nto sustainably replenish the CFE in this manner.\nIn 2020, approximately 40% of CFE allocations were \nrefunded (as at 22 April 2021). While low, it was higher \nthan in previous years (except for 2018). Figure 2 shows \nthe refund rate by year.\nThe re",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains that the fund was designed to be revolving but has been hard to replenish, with about 40% of 2020 allocations refunded. It notes that refunds vary by emergency, with most COVID-19 releases reimbursed but Ebola releases less so, and presents a table of releases and refunds by event.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/10665-342236/blocks/prose-sec-008",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "CFE contributions",
      "pageStart": 13,
      "pageEnd": 14,
      "target": "../sections/sec-008-cfe-contributions.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "In 2020, 13 Member States generously made contributions \nto the CFE totaling almost US$ 23 million (Table 3). \nAustria joined the list of contributors for the first time. \nContributions dropped from the previous two years. \nThis was likely to be as a result of the exceptional focus \nlast year on addressing and fully funding the COVID-19 \nresponse (Figure 3). See Annex 3 for a complete list \nof CFE contributors since 2015.\nTable 3  CFE contributions in 2020\nCountry\nContribution (US$)\nNetherlands\n 6 794 448 \nGermany\n 4 506 001 \nSweden\n 4 186 545 \nNorway\n 2 580 461 \nCanada\n 1 455 592 \nDenmark\n 1",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Reports that 13 Member States contributed nearly US$ 23 million in 2020, down from previous years likely because of the focus on funding COVID-19, with Austria joining for the first time. Tables and a chart show contributions by country and for 2015–2020, and the block notes how the fund enabled rapid responses amid multiple crises.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
